{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/973922-vampires-and-blindness","id":973922,"title":"Vampires and Blindness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-21T10:30:51-07:00","id":973922,"title":"Vampires and Blindness","content":"OK, so being blind as a bat means you have a -5 penalty on all rolls where vision is a factor, <i>and</i> your Defense is reduced to 0. Ouch.<br /> <br /> Which brings me to my battery of questions:<br /> <br /> 1. If I have Celerity, should I add the bonus <i>before</i> or <i>after</i> the modifiers for being blind? In other words, if I was entirely blind and had a dot of Celerity, should my Defense be 0 or 1?<br /> <br /> 2. If I have Auspex up, my Kindred Senses are stronger. Would that allow me to, say, aim by listening to heartbeats and sifting through smells, letting me punch someone without the &quot;can't see things&quot; penalty?<br /> <br /> 3. Would developing an Extra Sense through Protean \u2022\u2022 let me ignore all the penalties for being blind (i.e., I'd get my full Defense and no penalty on rolls), or would it just mitigate the penalty on rolls?<br /> <br /> 4. Dominate requires eye-contact - if I'm blind due to neurological damage or bad cataracts, am I still immune the way I'd be if I just straight-up didn't have eyes? Basically, does the symbolism of &quot;look into my eyes&quot; still work if you can't <i>look</i>?<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Put me on record as thinking that a blind Gangrel with a ghoul'd seeing-eye dog would be fun to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T10:49:24-07:00","id":973927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/973922-vampires-and-blindness#post973922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. If I have Celerity, should I add the bonus <i>before</i> or <i>after</i> the modifiers for being blind? In other words, if I was entirely blind and had a dot of Celerity, should my Defense be 0 or 1?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say you add it before the blind modifiers. Being faster doesn't help you avoid being hit if you can't see where the attacks are coming from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/973922-vampires-and-blindness#post973922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. If I have Auspex up, my Kindred Senses are stronger. Would that allow me to, say, aim by listening to heartbeats and sifting through smells, letting me punch someone without the &amp;quot;can't see things&amp;quot; penalty?</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds pretty cool, but beyond the scope of what Auspex and Kindred Senses usually do. Seems like good Devotion material to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/973922-vampires-and-blindness#post973922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Would developing an Extra Sense through Protean \u2022\u2022 let me ignore all the penalties for being blind (i.e., I'd get my full Defense and no penalty on rolls), or would it just mitigate the penalty on rolls?</div> </div> </div> </div>By a strict reading of RAW, it would only mitigate the penalty on rolls, but depending on the extra sense I might rule that it gives you back half or full Defense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/973922-vampires-and-blindness#post973922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. Dominate requires eye-contact - if I'm blind due to neurological damage or bad cataracts, am I still immune the way I'd be if I just straight-up didn't have eyes? Basically, does the symbolism of &amp;quot;look into my eyes&amp;quot; still work if you can't <i>look</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, 1e had a bloodline that was always blind, and many of them straight up didn't have eyes. They were not immune to Dominate, and could even use it themselves. Though, they did suffer I think a -2 dice penalty to their Dominate pools for trying to basically guess when their victim was looking at their eyes or where their eyes should be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/973922-vampires-and-blindness#post973922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Put me on record as thinking that a blind Gangrel with a ghoul'd seeing-eye dog would be fun to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>That does sound cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T11:22:14-07:00","id":973937,"title":"","content":"My take and/or experience on the matter. (I played an Ordo Dracul character who was blinded during her first chrysalis. She had a Russian black terrier for a seeing eye dog until he got killed by a rogue ghoul.)<br /> <br /> 1. Starting Defense is 0. In your example, Celerity would move it to 1 in most cases.<br /> 2. Your Auspex rating offsets the -5 penalty (Auspex 3 means the penalty is -2) If you have Blind Fighting as a specialty it would reduce the penalty accordingly. Ditto with a blind fighting merit. My character didn't go with a combat build but the option was there. But the penalty for sight still remains, it's just modified as a reflection that other senses are used in combat. <br /> 3. If you developed something like echolocation or tremor sense I'd run it as gradually your defense rating returns to standard and the penalty for blindness gradually goes away but no, it would not instantaneously go to factory defaults.<br /> 4. My character was fully blind, she never got special vision powers so she was immune to any applications of Dominate, Majesty, and Nightmare and devotions, psychic powers, merits etc. that required eye contact or for me to see the character to be affected. Those powers were also largely useless for her to use and others' obfuscate didn't work normally but still impacted relevant perception rolls. Others' line of sight powers would work and devotions that can channel blood sympathy and vinculums or contact with the power user's vitae to work instead of eye contact or visual onlooking allowed Dominate to work on her. And if she had gotten any power or ability to &quot;see&quot; that immunity would have been at least partially lost. That would be up to your ST to adjudicate. I'd advise you to check with him before assuming. If your ST likes to use a lot of visual and nonverbal imagery to impart clues like mine did, you can miss out on a lot of details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T12:07:24-07:00","id":973963,"title":"","content":"While I do agree being blind would cancel out dominate ( mainly because it specifically says so ) I would not have it cancel out Majesty or Nightmare as you do not need to see to be inspired, charmed, smitten, terrified or scared.. Nightmare and Majesty appeal to all senses.. not just the one. Also I dont see why if you were blind it would allow you not to use obfuscate. That is others looking upon you... not you looking at them. Though I could have read that part wrong. <br /> <br /> 1. I think celerity would help your defense so you could still use it. Getting out of the way isnt always about seeing it. sometimes it's about hearing it. If you were denied your defense because it was a surprise attack or something, then celerity wouldnt help anyway, but if you were talking and things were getting heated and you knew the attack might happen, then use it. <br /> <br /> 2. Narrative wise, I would allow you to do those things, but there are still too many factors involved and I think you would still get the negative. You could hear the heartbeat, you could pinpoint it, but that vase between the two of you is hindering the shot. You wouldnt be able to adjust for those things because you cant see or hear them. Negatives still apply. <br /> <br /> 3. I would think that echolocation would negate the blindness because now you are seeing differently. Not with eyeballs but with something else.<br /> <br /> 4. I think that if you have bad eyes and see total utter darkness, you would be immune, however, if you see fuzzy outlines, colors, lights or whatever, then you would not be immune. You dont need to see theirs, as it works through sunglasses. I think you just need to have some sort of vision .. my take on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T13:56:28-07:00","id":974014,"title":"","content":"1 &amp; 2.) Part of the Kindred can-operate-in-the-dark stuff is hearing compensating, so I'd say that a blind Kindred only suffers the partial Blindness penalty (-3 to rolls and half defense). I'd negate the penalties entirely for dealing with mortals within your heartbeat-hearing range. A vampire with the Acute Senses Merit can probably just negate the penalty entirely in all cases.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Relevant Bit of Blood and Smoke, Pg 91</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kindred do not suffer normal vision penalties for being in the<br /> dark, and can compensate with hearing. In full darkness, they<br /> only suffer a \u20132 die penalty to rolls that require vision.</div> </div> </div> </div>3.) I'd say that &quot;see without using her eyes&quot; would negate the penalty for operating with eyes that cannot see entirely, within a reasonable range for the sense - which can be derived from Kindred Senses ranges.<br /> <br /> 4.) The sidebar is &quot;can see your eyes -&gt; can be dominated&quot; so strictly speaking not being able to see would rule out Dominate, but that feels a little <i>blah, </i>y'know? I'd say that whatever could reasonably be called in-person eye contact is sufficient for Dominate to work; the point is a mystical link, etc. etc. This might mean that an eyeless Badacelli would still have to purposefully avert their gaze from a Ventrue threat, which is fine by me, really.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}